 "notes": "Headline measured limit is the \"DD current\" (observed, not the \"DD projected\" dashed) 95%-CL exclusion curve from Fig. 2b, the photon-coupling g_phigamma [eV^-1] plane (source file g_DM_gamma_gen_mass_5th_proj_no_title.pdf, a raster figure; boundary traced as the lower edge of the shaded excluded region by pixel analysis, axes calibrated from decade labels). Left/low-mass part is the d_alpha (fine-structure) bound; the transition near m~1e-10 eV (nu_step=50 kHz) switches to the 2d_alpha+d_me region. Chose the photon coupling (ScalarPhoton) over the electron coupling (Fig 2a, g_phie) as the flagship broad-range model-independent alpha bound; the paper reports both g_phie and g_phigamma symmetrically. Converted paper g_phigamma to Damour-Donoghue d_e via delta_alpha = g_phigamma <phi> alpha (Eq.2), i.e. d_e = g_phigamma/kappa with kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl=2.906e-19 GeV^-1: d_e = g_phigamma[eV^-1]*1e9/kappa = g_phigamma[eV^-1]*3.44e27 (log10 offset +27.54). Density: paper assumes rho_DM=3.1e-6 eV^4 ~ 0.40 GeV/cm^3 (local solar); bound scales as 1/sqrt(rho), reported at paper native density, not rescaled. Curve is the lower envelope (best exclusion reach); the raw curve is jagged (resonance losses) so single-column artifacts were median-smoothed. Physics cross-check: min g~1e-21 implies d_alpha~1e-13, matching Fig.1 deepest Delta f/f0.",
